{"thought": "The proposal to Finley is drafted behind a card; now I explain to Bob what Emery's link showed, why there's no Friday, and what Approve will send.", "tool": "tell_bob", "args": {"text": "Emery Ashby sent his booking link, and I read it: 24 open times over the next three weeks, but not a single Friday, so your Friday preference can't be met without going back to him empty-handed. Checking all 24 against your calendar, only Monday, Oct 19 holds anything in the lunch hour: 11:30am to 12:30pm, plus 11:00am to 12:00pm, which starts half an hour before your 11:30 to 1:30 lunch band. Everything else of his is either mid-afternoon, blocked on your side, or past what my calendar copy can see.

So I took your ask as a 60-minute in-person lunch on the north side, sometime in the next three weeks, Fridays preferred. The card as drafted is a note to Finley Bramley, you in cc, offering those two Monday, Oct 19 options; it introduces me, since nothing from me has reached them yet, and it says the 11:00am start sits outside your usual lunch window. It also notes that Emery's link has no Fridays open and that whoever has a favorite north-side spot can name it, since you left the place to them. Since Emery's times came from his own link, I'm not asking him for availability again, I'll confirm with him once Finley picks.

Approve sends that note to Finley; nothing goes out until you tap."}}
